## Production Concerns

| Concern | Fix |
|---|---|
| Thread blocks forever on a stuck pool | Use `wait_for` (timeouts), throw on expiry → return 503 |
| Pool grows unbounded | Cap capacity at construction; never create lazily without bounds |
| Stale/dead connections | Validate on checkout; discard + replace if dead |
| Slow startup | Trade-off: upfront init (default) vs. lazy init (race-prone) |
| Strict fairness | Use FIFO ordering structures; usually approximate FIFO is fine |
| Exception leaks a permit | Always `release` in `catch` / use RAII guard |

**Timeout heuristic:** typical op time × ~5. If a query is ~100 ms, set timeout to ~500 ms. Always shorter than your upstream load-balancer timeout.

